PracticeItems.Prompt:
Consider the following method:

public static String classify(int x, int y) {
    if (x > 0 && y > 0) {
        return "A";
    } else if (x > 0 || y > 0) {
        return "B";
    } else {
        return "C";
    }
}

What is returned by the call classify(-3, 5)?

Trace this code with a = 4, b = 8, c = 4:

if (a == b || (a == c && b > a)) {
    System.out.println("X");
} else if (a == c && !(b > a)) {
    System.out.println("Y");
} else {
    System.out.println("Z");
}

Which line is printed?

Given int score = 72; boolean passed = true; consider:

if (score >= 60 && passed) {
    System.out.println("Pass");
} else if (score >= 60 && !passed) {
    System.out.println("Disqualified");
} else {
    System.out.println("Fail");
}

What prints, and why does short-circuit evaluation matter for the second condition even though it isn't reached here?
